 {"id":"fabro-0195","title":"engine: declarative automation definitions in the repo (config/automations/*.toml) with on_overlap + breaker_threshold as code","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-06T21:41:21.610Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-06T21:41:21.610Z","description":"User review 2026-09-06 ('warum ist der skip nicht in der workflow def gesetzt?'): the conductor automation exists ONLY as live DB state — hand-created via UI/API, on_overlap never set (default Fire caused the three-pass stacking night), breaker_threshold likewise unset. Nothing versioned declares the line's safety posture; a DB reset or re-created automation silently loses skip/threshold and re-exposes the stacking + breaker-less behavior. The legacy import path (import_legacy_directory_once, dir = <config>/automations) exists but the repo ships no files there and import is one-shot legacy-shaped. Wanted: declarative automation definitions (e.g. config/automations/conductor.toml: target, workflow, environment, schedule expression, on_overlap=skip, breaker_threshold) that are (a) reviewed in PRs, (b) reconciled on server start (upsert by id; live pause state PRESERVED — enabled flag stays operator-owned, like today's resume flow), (c) surfaced in the web UI as 'managed from repo'. The workflow.fabro itself cannot carry on_overlap (scheduler-scope, not graph-scope) — the seed is about the automation layer getting its own source of truth. Interim (applied live 2026-09-06): on_overlap=skip set via API on the conductor.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-3b1b","title":"sandbox: openapi-generator-cli needs java — regen fails in runs, implementer hand-edits the generated TS client (live drift on denkhaus)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T07:48:54.498Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T07:48:54.498Z","description":"Evidence (develop run 01M1VZTJSZ551NFPHPXD429MG0, implementer, 2026-09-06): 'bun run generate' for lib/packages/fabro-api-client fails in run sandboxes because openapi-generator-cli requires java, which is NOT in the fabro-toolchain image. The implementer worked around it by HAND-EDITING the generated lib/packages/fabro-api-client/src/models/automation-schedule-trigger.ts 'to mirror generator output' — that hand-edit merged to denkhaus via PR #32: the checked-in generated client is now unverified drift; the next regen on a java-capable machine may churn or silently differ. Fix directions: (a) hermetic regen — add a JRE to the fabro-toolchain image OR switch generation to a java-less path (e.g. hey-api/openapi-ts via bun) so 'bun run generate' runs in every sandbox; (b) reconcile the drift: regenerate canonically once java/hermetic regen exists and commit the canonical output; (c) develop prompts + gate must treat lib/packages/fabro-api-client/src as GENERATED: hand edits are a process defect — the gate should diff generated output or at least flag manual edits to generated paths.","labels":["sandbox","workflows","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-febd","title":"qualitygate: fabro-server graph-render tests need target/debug/fabro — gate only builds touched crates and fails 3 tests deterministically","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T07:49:03.612Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T07:49:03.612Z","description":"Evidence (develop run 01M1VZTJSZ551NFPHPXD429MG0, tester stage, 2026-09-06): scripts/qualitygate.nu gates only the touched crates, but fabro-server graph-render unit tests (server::tests::get_graph_returns_svg, render_graph_from_manifest_*) invoke target/debug/fabro. When a run touches fabro-server WITHOUT fabro-cli in the touched set, the binary is missing and the gate fails 3 tests deterministically — the 01M1VZTJSZ55 run burned a whole implementer revisit on this. Fix directions: (a) qualitygate builds 'cargo build -p fabro-cli --bin fabro' whenever fabro-server is in the touched set (make the dependency explicit in the gate recipe), or (b) the tests skip with a clear skip message when the binary is absent (worse: hides real regressions), or (c) decouple the tests from the CLI binary via a test-support builder. Prefer (a).","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
-{"id":"fabro-bde4","title":"engine: fabro_run_wait until=merged needs a gate-failure signal — OPEN PR with failed checks must not loop timeouts forever","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T09:42:18.217Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T09:42:18.217Z","description":"Incident 2026-09-07 (conductor pass 01M1XCC9SP1YH38326ZCVJZT3J, develop child 01M1XCHJTDBJKZ31VFMY1KD61Q, PR #33): the develop child merged its work and enabled auto-merge, but the dogfood gate FAILED and a later base push made the PR DIRTY. The conductor leg waits with fabro_run_wait until=merged; ADR-0016 wait results are terminal|merged|closed_unmerged|timeout — a PR that is OPEN with failed checks (or DIRTY) matches NONE of them, so every wait returns timeout and the agent re-waits: 5 chained fabro_run_wait calls over 2+ hours with zero routing until manual repair (debug!-level fix + base merge pushed to the run branch, 09:3x UTC). Wanted: (a) the wait result gains a distinct reached value (e.g. 'blocked' or 'checks_failed') when the linked PR is open but its required checks concluded FAILURE, or its merge state is DIRTY/BLOCKED for a sustained window; (b) conductor prompts route that value to a repair child or park with a clear reason instead of re-waiting; (c) regression test: open PR + failed checks + until=merged returns the new value, not timeout. Related: fabro-94e8 (auto-rebase for stale bases), fabro-6a77 (branch-pushed-PR-failed completion semantics), ADR-0016.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
